    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nUser highlights `%1*,...,%9*` are a poor man's version of #29976 that allows highlights to adapt to the difference between current and non-current status line. But it is less user-friendly and has only been implemented for the status line and a small subset of highlight groups: `User1`, ..., `User9`.\n\nIt works by computing the difference between `StatusLine` and `User[1-9]`, and applying it to `StatusLineNC`. In the following Vim example, the current status line's background has to be repeated in the user highlight to make this work:\n```sh\nvim --clean +\"hi StatusLine NONE ctermbg=green | hi StatusLineNC NONE ctermbg=blue | hi User1 ctermbg=green ctermfg=red | set stl=default\\ %1*user | sp\"\n```\nSince Neovim 0.12, this feature (and having to repeat the background) has become redundant, because all status line highlights are automatically combined with `StatusLine[NC]` anyway:\n```sh\nnvim --clean +\"hi StatusLine guibg=green | hi StatusLineNC guibg=blue | hi User1 guifg=red | set stl=default\\ %1*user | sp\"\n```\nNot only is it redundant, there are also problems with the implementation:\n- The mechanism is hard-coded to only work properly for 'statusline' despite also being active for 'ruler', 'tabline', and 'winbar', and it is ignored for 'statuscolumn', where all user highlights are mapped to `Normal`.\n- Already in Vim, user highlights don't follow links.\n- Unlike in Vim, user highlights in the non-current status line don't work when `StatusLineNC` is defined from scratch with `hi StatusLineNC NONE ...`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUser highlights not following links:\n```sh\nnvim --clean +\"hi StatusLine guibg=green | hi StatusLineNC guibg=blue | hi User1 guifg=red | hi link User2 User1 | set stl=default\\ %1*user\\ %2*link | sp\"\n```\n`StatusLineNC` defined from scratch:\n```sh\nnvim --clean +\"hi StatusLine NONE guibg=green | hi StatusLineNC NONE guibg=blue | hi User1 guifg=red | set stl=default\\ %1*user | sp\"\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI propose to make `%1*,...,%9*` equivalent to `%#User1#,...,%#User9#`, in other words just a convenient abbreviation.\n\nThis is a breaking change, users will have to remove the user highlight attributes repeated from `StatusLine`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\npartly\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS 26.05\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ntmux-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
